# Change Discipline

## Before coding

1. Identify which pillar(s) are affected (Core / Overlay / Research).
2. Check existing patterns — extend before inventing.
3. If touching offsets: Research probe first, then `Poe2Offsets`, then readers.

## While coding

- **Big features:** use a feature branch → `dotnet test` → merge to `main` locally (see `git-workflow.mdc`).
- **One concern per commit/PR** when possible.
- Don't edit `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, or `README.md` unless asked.
- Don't add dependencies without strong justification (keep publish size lean).
- Don't remove gamepad or perf safeguards when adding features.

## Feature completion checklist

- [ ] Core/Overlay/Research boundary respected
- [ ] Settings + migration + API + ImGui (if user-facing)
- [ ] Tooltip/hint in `SettingHints` + ImGui + dashboard (if user-facing control)
- [ ] Keyboard + gamepad (if bindable)
- [ ] Perf: cadence/sleep, no hot-path LINQ
- [ ] Unit test for pure logic / migration
- [ ] `dotnet build` succeeds (x64)

## Refactors

Only when they directly enable the task. No "cleanup" sweeps across unrelated files.

## Versioning

`UpdateChecker` / assembly version for release builds — bump when user-visible release ships (don't bump casually on every commit).
